Calls: the queue of the other side's voice grows when the sound server takes more than it holds.
PulseAudio on the FuriLabs FLX1s (droid sink) takes 40-60 ms of sound at once every ~45 ms, while the
OpenAL device module keeps only 5 buffers of 10 ms: the source ran dry several times a second, a click
each time. It starts with 5 as before and keeps what was taken in one pass plus 4 buffers (up to 16).

